        "description": "Why does Rome loom so large in the popular mindset – arguably more so than any other ancient civilisation – and what can that reveal about how we understand the past? Emily Briffett speaks with historian Rhiannon Garth Jones about her book All Roads Lead to Rome, to explore how the idea of Rome has been endlessly reused, reshaped and repurposed from ancient empire to modern politics and pop culture. Together, they consider the question: does Rome still matter today? ----- GO BEYOND THE PODCAST Curious to find out more about the Abbasid caliphate mentioned in the episode? Check out this episode with Hugh Kennedy, where he answers your questions on the multicultural medieval caliphate that stretched from Tunisia to the frontiers of India: https://bit.ly/3Q5Jcee ----- GET MORE WITH MEMBERSHIP Become a HistoryExtra podcast member and unlock access to The Full Story podcast, plus enjoy ad-free listening, early access to other podcast episodes, and a member-exclusive newsletter. Find out more and sign up here: ⁠https://historyextra.supportingcast.fm⁠ ----- EXPLORE MORE For more fascinating stories from the past, head to HistoryExtra, the home of ‘History’s Greatest’ podcasts. Find out more at ⁠⁠⁠historyextra.com/podcast⁠⁠⁠. ----- GET IN TOUCH We'd love to know what you think about the podcast, so leave us a review and let us know the topics you think we should be covering. Or, follow us on ⁠Facebook⁠, ⁠X⁠, ⁠Instagram⁠ or ⁠YouTube⁠ to keep in touch. Learn more about your ad choices. Visit podcastchoices.com/adchoices",
